<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>1.12.7: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00275</md:content-id>
    <md:title>1.12.7: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>0ee0ff6d-38af-4147-8576-3dec7682c402</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<para>In 1 - 2, find the equation of a line with given slope and \( y \)-intercept. Write the equation in slope-intercept form.</para>
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="c3e16583-349e-4429-bc29-2d8c38bd2463" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="2" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <!--Enter Questions Below this line-->
  <!--Q1-->
  <exercise data-content-id="8ef284c1-00ab-48a5-88e3-a507f9d890c1" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(y=3x+5\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(y=5x+3\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y=3x+0\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y=3x+5\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y=0x+3\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>slope 3 and \( y \)-intercept \( ( 0,5) \)</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \( y=3x+5 \) 
        \(\begin{array}{rcl}y-y_1&amp;=&amp;m(x-x_1)\\y-(5)&amp;=&amp;3(x-(0))\\y-5&amp;=&amp;3(x)\\y-5&amp;=&amp;3x\\y&amp;=&amp;3x+5\\&amp;&amp;\end{array}\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.12.2.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  
  <!--Q2-->
  <exercise data-content-id="d44ab61a-84e5-4c4c-822b-3016c0730bf5" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(y=-3x-1\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(y=-x-3\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y=-3x-1\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y=-x+0\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y=0x-3\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>slope \(−3 \) and \( y \)-intercept \( (0,−1)\)</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \( y=-3x-1 \)</para>
      <para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}y-y_1&amp;=&amp;m(x-x_1)\\y-(-1)&amp;=&amp;-3(x-(0))\\y+1&amp;=&amp;-3(x)\\y+1&amp;=&amp;-3x\\y&amp;=&amp;-3x-1\end{array}\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.12.2.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  
  <!--Q3-->
  <exercise data-content-id="22534ea5-e0df-44bb-82b5-d457a01de3a3" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(y=3x-5\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(y=-3x+5\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y=5x-3\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y=-5x+3\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y=3x-5\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>In 3 - 4, Choose the slope-intercept form of the equation of the line, shown in each graph. </para>
      <para>
          <figure><media alt=""><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/09a02347b18374d51af8598355f5cf5524859116"/></media></figure></para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \( y=3x-5 \)</para>
      <para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}m&amp;=&amp;\frac{y_2-y_1}{x_2-x_1}\\m&amp;=&amp;\frac{(1)-(-2)}{(2)-(1)}\\m&amp;=&amp;\frac{1+2}{2-1}\\m&amp;=&amp;\frac{3}{1}=3\end{array}\)</para>
      <para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}y−y_1&amp;=&amp;m(x−x_1)\\y−(−2)&amp;=&amp;3(x−(1))\\y+2&amp;=&amp;3(x−1)\\y+2&amp;=&amp;3x−3\\y&amp;=&amp;3x−5\end{array}\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.12.2.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  
  <!--Q4-->
  <exercise data-content-id="b4b0e8cb-bca8-4efe-860f-165f82fd0d0f" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(y=-2x+4\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(y=-2x+4\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y=2x+4\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y=\\frac12x -4\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y=\\frac12 x+2\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>
          <figure><media alt=""><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/eeae77b746d027b94298de1aaee697496e0d56a5"/></media></figure></para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \( y=-2x+4 \)</para>
      <para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}m&amp;=&amp;\frac{y_2-y_1}{x_2-x_1}\\m&amp;=&amp;\frac{(4)-(0)}{(0)-(2)}\\m&amp;=&amp;\frac{4-0}{0-2}\\m&amp;=&amp;\frac{4}{-2}&amp;=&amp;-2\end{array}\)</para>
      <para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}y − y_1 &amp;=&amp; m(x − x_1)\\y − (0) &amp;=&amp; −2(x − (2))\\y &amp;=&amp; −2(x − 2)\\y &amp;=&amp; −2x + 4\end{array}\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.12.2.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  
  <!--Q5-->
  <exercise data-content-id="a0d8a289-e8c3-4a6f-b6aa-febc913fcfa0" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(y=-7x-10\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(y=-7x-1\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y=-7x-3\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y=-3x+10\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y=-7x-10\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Choose the equation of a line with the given
          slope and containing the given point that best represents the line in
          slope-intercept form. </para>
      <para> \(m=−7\), point \((−1,−3)\)</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \( y=-7x-10 \)</para>
      <para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}y − y_1 &amp;=&amp; m(x − x_1)\\y − (−3) &amp;=&amp; −7(x − (−1))\\y + 3 &amp;=&amp; −7(x + 1)\\y + 3 &amp;=&amp; −7x − 7\\y &amp;=&amp; −7x − 10\end{array}\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.12.2.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  
  <!--Q6-->
  <exercise data-content-id="988663d2-d0e1-4007-a583-801276ebffbe" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(y=-\frac72x+4\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(y=-\\frac72x-3\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y=\\frac72x+4\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y=-\\frac27x+4\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y=-\\frac72x+4\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Choose the equation of a line containing the given points that best
          represents the line in slope-intercept form. </para>
      <para> \((0,4)\) and \((2,−3)\)</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(y=-\frac72x+4\)</para>
      <para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}m&amp;=&amp;\frac{y_2-y_1}{x_2-x_1}\\m&amp;=&amp;\frac{(-3)-(4)}{(2)-(0)}\\m&amp;=&amp;\frac{-3-4}{2-0}\\m&amp;=&amp;\frac{-7}{2}\end{array}\)</para>
      <para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}y − y_1 &amp;=&amp; m(x − x_1)\\y − (4) &amp;=&amp; -\frac{7}{2}(x − (0))\\y − 4 &amp;=&amp; -\frac{7}{2}(x)\\y &amp;=&amp; -\frac{7}{2}x + 4\end{array}\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.12.4.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  
  <!--Q7-->
  <exercise data-content-id="1ddea227-6cfa-401e-9c34-d66382305700" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(y=-4\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(y=-4\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y=0\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(x=2\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(x=-2\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Choose the equation of a line containing the given points
          that best represents the line in slope-intercept form.</para>
      <para>\((3,−4)\) and \((5,−4)\)</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(y=-4\)</para>
      <para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}m&amp;=&amp;\frac{y_2-y_1}{x_2-x_1}\\m&amp;=&amp;\frac{(-4)-(-4)}{(5)-(3)}\\m&amp;=&amp;\frac{-4+4}{5-3}\\m&amp;=&amp;\frac{0}{2}=0\end{array}\)</para>
      <para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}y − y_1 &amp;=&amp; m(x − x_1)\\y − (−4) &amp;=&amp; 0(x − (3))\\y + 4 &amp;=&amp; 0(x − 3)\\y &amp;=&amp; −4\end{array}\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.12.4.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  
  <!--Q#-->
  <exercise data-content-id="0d4df168-9815-422a-b8fe-790cdafe44fc" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(3x - y =1\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(y=3x-1\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(-3x+y = -1 \\)&quot;, &quot;\\(3x - y =1\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y=3x -11\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Which of the following equations is 
          \(y-5=3(x-2)\) written in standard form? </para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!</para>
      <para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}y-5&amp;=&amp;3(x-2)\\y-5&amp;=&amp;3x-6\\y-5+5&amp;=&amp;3x-6+5\\y&amp;=&amp;3x-1\\y-3x&amp;=&amp;3x-3x-1\\-3x +y&amp;=&amp;-1\\\frac{-3x}{ -1}+\frac{y}{-1}&amp;=&amp;{-1}{-1}\\3x - y &amp;=&amp;1\end{array}\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.12.4.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q#9-->
  <exercise data-content-id="c345c099-f334-4829-a6f2-07a7c7ebcf82" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-solution="\(y-2=3(x-4)\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(y-2=3(x-4)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y-4=-3(x+2)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y+2=\\frac13(x-4)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y-4=3(x-2)\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Write the equation of a line that contains the points \((–3,–1)\) and \((2,–2)\). Write the equation in point-slope form.</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Q#10-->
  <exercise data-content-id="1793fb44-9898-4e66-9783-3eb4a0f4b282" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-solution="\(8x-y=19\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(8x - y = -19 \\)&quot;, &quot;\\(8x + y = 19\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(8x-y=19\\)&quot;, &quot;\\( 19x + y = 8\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Write the equation of a line that contains the point (2, -3) with a slope of 8. Write the equation in standard form.</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Q#11-->
  <exercise data-content-id="545e7634-a60f-48dc-aa3e-fc69ccc363d6" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-solution="\(x+y=4\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(x - y = 4 \\)&quot;, &quot;\\(x+y=4\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(-x+y = 4\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(x + y = -4\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Write the equation of a line that contains the points (3, 1) and (-1, 5). Write the equation in standard form. </para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
